{
  "category": "Big-Hearted Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "It rescues people stranded by blizzards in the mountains. Its shaggy fur shields it from the cold.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "This extremely wise Pokémon excels at rescuing people stranded at sea or in the mountains.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "Being wrapped in its long fur is so comfortable that a person would be fine even overnight on a wintry mountain.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Being wrapped in its long fur is so comfortable that a person would be fine even overnight on a wintry mountain.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "It rescues people stranded by blizzards in the mountains. Its shaggy fur shields it from the cold.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "Being wrapped in its long fur is so comfortable that a person would be fine even overnight on a wintry mountain.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "It rescues people stranded by blizzards in the mountains. Its shaggy fur shields it from the cold.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Being wrapped in its long fur is so comfortable that a person would be fine even overnight on a wintry mountain.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Intelligent, good-natured, and valiant, it’s a trustworthy partner on rescue teams.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "With this wise Pokémon, there could be no concern that it would ever attack people. Some parents even trust it to babysit.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It pays no mind to the cold, thanks to its long warm coat. Stoutland in Alola look a little uncomfortable.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its fur is long and thick. A long time ago in cold regions, every household kept a Stoutland.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "These Pokémon seem to enjoy living with humans. Even a Stoutland caught in the wild will warm up to people in about three days.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stoutland is immensely proud of its impressive moustache. It’s said that moustache length is what determines social standing among this species.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
